        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Change a standard or Stream Brita filter every 40 gallons or about two months, and an Elite every 120 gallons or about six months, whichever comes first. Work out your real schedule from how often you refill, change sooner in hard water, and believe your taste over the indicator.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If you filter for taste, the standard filter changed on time does the job cheaply. If you filter for lead, use a filter certified for it and follow the gallon count strictly. And if you are filtering gallons a day, it may be time to look beyond a pitcher; our <a href="/best-water-filter-pitcher/" class="text-[#1E90FF] font-semibold hover:underline">best water filter pitchers</a> guide is a good place to compare.
